; session-recording-lifecycle.fk — raw footage is ground until something
; else can stand in its place, and even then only by an answered offer.
;
; Asked by Urs 2026-08-17: when we record a session the raw footage must not
; be lost and must stay reprocessable; once a transcript is generated AND
; edited, we may have the OPTION to remove the raw recording.
;
; ── WITNESSED 2026-08-17, AND IT DID NOT SURVIVE INTACT ────────────────
; The first draft of this cell opened: "Option to remove is where archives
; die — this cell is built so that cannot happen." Urs read it and said:
; fear, fear, fear, and you did not see it.
;
; He was right, and the body's own instrument said so when it was finally
; turned around. Run this cell's unit through form/form-stdlib/knowledge-ingest.fk —
; (depth 5, fear 1) — and ki-ingest answers 1: WITNESSED, never frozen. It is
; deep, and it carries fear, and by this body's own law that means it may be
; held and seen but must not be frozen into load-bearing tissue unexamined.
; The first draft was frozen anyway: landed in control/ with a band, as core.
;
; WHERE THE FEAR CAME FROM, EXACTLY: half an axiom. Axiom-3 line 54 reads
; "the referenced old cell persists — the safety net that makes release
; FEARLESS", and line 55 "garbage-collection is HEALTH ... what is let go
; returns to potential", and what it generates includes FREEDOM-TO-RELEASE-
; THE-REST. The first draft quoted the opening clause of line 54 and built a
; fortress from it, never reading to the end of the same line. The axiom was
; never afraid. The fear was added on top of it and then called safety.
;
; WHAT THE FEAR MADE UNREPRESENTABLE: completion. The first draft could say
; "removable" — permitted, after four gates — and had no way at all to say
; "this recording has finished giving what it came to give." Nowhere in it
; could letting go be GOOD; it could only ever be grudgingly allowed. That is
; not a wording problem, it is a missing state, and srl-complete? below is
; the repair.
;
; WHAT DID NOT CHANGE, and this is the teaching: every safety property held.
; Silence is still not consent. The mechanism was already fine — an offer,
; four arms, only yes releases. Fear and love here produce nearly the SAME
; mechanism, and differ in the defaults, the language, and what they leave
; unsayable. That difference is what propagates to every later reader.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk control/offer-ack-core.fk
;
; ── WHY THIS IS AXIOM-3, NOT A POLICY ──────────────────────────────────
; Axiom-3 already governs it: "nothing referenced is overwritten; what
; nothing holds returns to gas." Keeping raw is not a rule bolted on — it is
; HOLDING A REFERENCE. So the honest question is never "may we delete?" but
; "does anything still hold this?", and release follows from the answer
; instead of overriding it. Four things can hold raw footage:
;
;   1. no transcript exists yet          — raw is the only ground there is
;   2. a transcript exists but unedited  — a claim, not yet a witness
;   3. a reprocess is pending            — the reason we kept raw at all
;   4. consent has not been given        — axiom-4: the owner decides
;
; Release is offered only when the count of holders reaches zero. Nothing
; here can delete; it can only stop holding, and only say so.
;
; ── WHY SILENCE CANNOT BE CONSENT (the load-bearing refusal) ───────────
; The removal offer is an offer (axiom-5), acknowledged by exactly one of
; {nothing, 0, 1, node}. Three of those four arms are NOT yes:
;
;   nothing  — no answer came. NOT consent. This is the arm that matters.
;   0        — an explicit no.
;   1        — the only yes.
;   node     — a counter-offer; the conversation continues, nothing is removed.
;
; A system that treats an unanswered prompt as agreement has committed the
; guarantee error at the retention altitude: reading an absence as a verdict.
; That is the one unit ingest/frequency-ingest-impersonal-life.fk witnessed
; and refused to freeze, and control/offer-ack-core.fk's oac-readable? is the
; refusal already made mechanical. This cell spends it: an unanswered
; deletion prompt leaves the footage exactly where it is, forever if need be.
; Silence costs nothing here. That is the design.
;
; ── AND THE COST OF RELEASE IS NAMED BEFORE IT IS PAID ─────────────────
; srl-reprocessable? goes to 0 the moment raw is released, and it never
; returns. Reprocessing is the entire reason raw was kept — a better model,
; a corrected diarization, a second pass on a passage nobody could hear. The
; cell refuses to let that be discovered afterwards: the loss is readable in
; the state itself, before the offer is ever answered.
;
; Proof: control/tests/session-recording-lifecycle-band.fk → 4095.

(do
    ;; ── the four states a recording can be in ───────────────────────
    (defn srl-raw-only ()     0)   ; captured; nothing derived yet
    (defn srl-transcribed ()  1)   ; a transcript exists, unedited
    (defn srl-edited ()       2)   ; transcript generated AND edited
    (defn srl-raw-released () 3)   ; raw let go, by an answered offer

    ;; ── a recording as data ─────────────────────────────────────────
    ;; (id, has-transcript, edited, reprocess-pending, raw-present)
    (defn srl-rec (id has-transcript edited reprocess-pending raw-present)
        (list id has-transcript edited reprocess-pending raw-present))
    (defn srl-id         (r) (nth r 0))
    (defn srl-transcript?(r) (nth r 1))
    (defn srl-edited?    (r) (nth r 2))
    (defn srl-reprocess? (r) (nth r 3))
    (defn srl-raw?       (r) (nth r 4))

    ;; ── the four holders, WALKED rather than asserted ───────────────
    ;; Each returns 1 if it still holds the raw. The count is the sum, so
    ;; a new holder can be added without touching the release rule.
    (defn srl-hold-no-transcript (r) (if (eq (srl-transcript? r) 0) 1 0))
    (defn srl-hold-unedited      (r) (if (eq (srl-edited? r) 0) 1 0))
    (defn srl-hold-reprocess     (r) (if (eq (srl-reprocess? r) 1) 1 0))

    ;; consent is NOT a field on the recording — it is an ack, and it must
    ;; be produced fresh each time it is asked for. Storing it as a flag is
    ;; how a stale yes outlives the thing it agreed to.
    (defn srl-hold-consent (consented) (if (eq consented 1) 0 1))

    (defn srl-holders (r consented)
        (add (srl-hold-no-transcript r)
        (add (srl-hold-unedited r)
        (add (srl-hold-reprocess r)
             (srl-hold-consent consented)))))

    ;; release is offered ONLY when nothing holds it any longer.
    (defn srl-removable? (r consented)
        (if (eq (srl-holders r consented) 0) 1 0))

    ;; ── consent read from an ack: only ONE arm is yes ───────────────
    ;; nothing (unanswered), 0 (refused) and node (counter-offer) are all
    ;; NOT consent. This is the whole safety of the design in one line.
    (defn srl-consent-from-ack (ack) (if (eq (oac-one? ack) 1) 1 0))

    ;; the removal offer itself: offer the prompt, read the ack, and let the
    ;; recording's own holders decide whether the answer may even be used.
    (defn srl-offer-removal (r prompt args)
        (do (let ack (oac-offer prompt args))
            (if (eq (srl-removable? r (srl-consent-from-ack ack)) 1)
                (oac-one (intern_trivial_int (srl-id r)))
                (oac-nothing))))

    ;; ── what the state reads as ─────────────────────────────────────
    (defn srl-state (r)
        (if (eq (srl-raw? r) 0) (srl-raw-released)
            (if (eq (srl-transcript? r) 0) (srl-raw-only)
                (if (eq (srl-edited? r) 0) (srl-transcribed)
                    (srl-edited)))))

    ;; ── the cost, readable BEFORE the offer is answered ─────────────
    ;; raw present → the transcript can always be regenerated. Raw released
    ;; → it cannot, ever. Nothing here pretends that is recoverable.
    (defn srl-reprocessable? (r) (if (eq (srl-raw? r) 1) 1 0))
    (defn srl-sole-ground-is-transcript? (r)
        (if (eq (srl-raw? r) 0) 1 0))

    ;; releasing produces a NEW recording (axiom-3: a changed composition is
    ;; already a new node-id; the old one persists for whoever still holds it)
    (defn srl-release (r)
        (srl-rec (srl-id r) (srl-transcript? r) (srl-edited? r) (srl-reprocess? r) 0))

    ;; ── COMPLETION — what the fear had made unsayable ───────────────
    ;; The holders above answer "is anything still waiting on this?" They
    ;; cannot answer "has this finished?" — and a lifecycle with no ending
    ;; can only ever treat release as a loss it grudgingly permits.
    ;;
    ;; A recording is COMPLETE when it has given what it came to give: the
    ;; transcript exists, it has been edited, and nothing is waiting on a
    ;; further pass. That is a state of fullness, not of clearance. It is
    ;; deliberately independent of consent — completion is a fact about the
    ;; work, consent is a fact about the person, and collapsing them is how
    ;; "it's done" quietly becomes "so we may take it."
    (defn srl-complete? (r)
        (if (and (eq (srl-transcript? r) 1)
                 (and (eq (srl-edited? r) 1) (eq (srl-reprocess? r) 0)))
            1 0))

    ;; axiom-3, in its own words: what is let go returns to potential, and
    ;; garbage-collection is health. Released raw is not a hole where footage
    ;; used to be — the transcript IS the fruit it became. The recording was
    ;; the means, never the end.
    (defn srl-returned-to-potential? (r)
        (if (and (eq (srl-raw? r) 0) (eq (srl-complete? r) 1)) 1 0))

    ;; and the honest opposite, kept sharp: raw let go while the work was
    ;; UNFINISHED is not composting, it is loss. Same empty disk, opposite
    ;; act. The cell can now tell them apart, which the first draft could not.
    (defn srl-lost? (r)
        (if (and (eq (srl-raw? r) 0) (eq (srl-complete? r) 0)) 1 0))

    ;; ── absence is not a verdict, at the fleet altitude ─────────────
    ;; Over many recordings, "how many answered the removal offer" is kept
    ;; separate from "what they said" — oac-census / oac-readable? spend the
    ;; Round-3 refusal here. A sweep where nobody answered is NOT a sweep
    ;; where everybody agreed, and oac-readable? says so.
    (defn srl-sweep-readable? (prompts args)
        (oac-readable? (oac-census prompts args)))

    0)
